# Browser
# Backup 1 (CR 702.165a) on another creature, cast on turn three so Ornithopter can attack the turn the ability lasts:
# Ornithopter (0/2) gets the counter (1/3) and the ability until end of turn, and its face says so, so it hits for its toughness
# 3 (CR 510.1a), not its power 1: 20 - 3. Negotiator keeps the ability (the rulings), and has no counter. On turn five the
# granted ability is gone and the counter stays: Ornithopter hits for its power 1, and Negotiator, a 0/2 that would assign
# nothing by power, for its toughness 2: 17 - 3.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Mox Pearl
Ornithopter
Streetwise Negotiator
Plains x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x15

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Streetwise Negotiator.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Target(Ornithopter)
Bot1.Attack(Ornithopter > Bot2)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot2.Life = 17
? Bot1.Battlefield.Streetwise Negotiator.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = (absent)
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Keywords = AssignsDamageByToughness; Flying
? Client.Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Rules = Flying / This creature assigns combat damage equal to its toughness rather than its power.
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Keywords = Flying
? Client.Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Rules = Flying
Bot1.Attack(Ornithopter; Streetwise Negotiator > Bot2)
[T5 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot2.Life = 14

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Power = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Toughness = 3
Bot1.Battlefield.Streetwise Negotiator.Keywords = AssignsDamageByToughness
